  "decision": "Patched: dynamo-default-cost-fn accepts parameters.seed (u64), which seeds tie-breaks and softmax sampling over candidates in worker order. The harness must express the default baseline as YAML type dynamo-default-cost-fn with a seed, never the no-YAML builtin default. Canonical-determinism mode (ordinal UUIDs) was not exposed in the Python API because UUIDs do not affect outcomes. The harness compares per-request rows as a sorted multiset without uuid and recomputes metrics from per_request; it must not compare native mean/std fields bit-for-bit.",
  "noise_floor_correction": "Added by setup fixer r0 (audit F1). Superseded guidance: identical re-runs and tie seeds alone do not measure noise; rr, lmetric, two-tier and seeded default are deterministic per workload, yet the arbitrary order of simultaneous arrivals moves per-cell goodput 1.2-3.9% CV for every policy. Noise is measured only from CRN workload replicates (protocol crn-order-v1). See facts/noise.json.",
